The checks of tests/network: each is run by the system, as root, in an
empty directory, once it has a user guest with the password Gu3st-pw and
a user ftp, and must write what follows its "--", to the byte
(tests/harness/checks.py).  The first names the machine, brings its
Ethernet interface up and has inetd start the three daemons that
/etc/inetd.conf has commented out; the rest rely on it.  It starts
sendmail's daemon too, which /etc/rc.conf leaves off, for its SMTP
server: once the machine has its name, which sendmail takes as it
starts.

The checks of mail come last, since they leave mail in guest's home
directory.  A letter is shown less the lines that differ from one run
to the next: the date and the queue's name for it.  A letter from root
is postmarked "From daemon": sendmail runs no mailer as root, but as
daemon, and names the sender to /bin/mail only when it was named to
sendmail.  A configuration sendmail has frozen is one it can thaw
without the file it was read from.

